  "result": "Perfect! All 126 tests pass. Here's a summary of the VAT implementation:\n\n**Added to src/invoices.js:**\n- `lineVat(line)` function: Calculates VAT on each line as (lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate \u00f7 100, rounded to whole cents\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n  - Sums line VATs (per-line calculation, not invoice-wide percentage)\n  - total = subtotal - discount + vat\n  - All amounts clamped at 0\n\n**Updated src/render.js:**\n- Shows VAT on its own line in rendered invoices, just above the total\n- Only displays VAT line if VAT > 0\n\n**Test Coverage:**\n- 16 new VAT tests covering:\n  - lineVat calculations with different VAT rates (0%, 9%, 21%)\n  - lineVat on discounted amounts\n  - invoiceTotals with VAT\n  - Multiple lines with different VAT rates\n  - Discount and VAT combinations\n  - Total clamping at 0\n  \n- 7 render tests verifying:\n  - VAT line display\n  - VAT position above total\n  - No VAT line for 0% VAT products\n  - Total includes VAT\n\n**Key design:**\n- VAT is computed **per line** on the line's amount after discount, not on invoice totals\n- Each line's VAT is rounded independently before summing\n- Invoice's VAT is the sum of all rounded line VATs\n\nAll 126 tests pass successfully, with proper banker's rounding throughout.",
